From 67d5347d94b4118bb7b0141c626111448a1e3f8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antonio Borneo <antonio.borneo@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Jun 2026 17:32:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] bus: rifsc: drop device links while detaching the node

When a peripheral cannot be accessed, the firewall detach its node
so it will not be probed.
But the device links supplier/consumers of the node are still in
place and the device link framework will issue an error when will
update such links due to the probe of a supplier or a provider of
the node.

	stm32-rifsc 42080000.bus: Failed to create device link (0x180) with supplier soc@0:pinctrl@44240000 for /soc@0/bus@42080000/i2c@40130000

Drop the links supplier/consumers while detaching the node.

Signed-off-by: Antonio Borneo <antonio.borneo@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I49227ad1f8cebc663bdf1697e2dcf6ff081810be
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/573868
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
---
 drivers/bus/stm32_rifsc.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bus/stm32_rifsc.c b/drivers/bus/stm32_rifsc.c
index 7ddcf97957bc..73efd5ac9863 100644
--- a/drivers/bus/stm32_rifsc.c
+++ b/drivers/bus/stm32_rifsc.c
@@ -785,8 +785,11 @@ static int stm32_rifsc_populate_bus(struct stm32_firewall_controller *ctrl)
 			if (err) {
 				/*
 				 * Peripheral access not allowed or not defined.
-				 * Mark the node as populated so platform bus won't probe it
+				 * Mark the node as populated so platform bus won't probe it.
+				 * Drop the links supplier/consumers to prevent device link
+				 * to query the node.
 				 */
+				fwnode_links_purge(of_fwnode_handle(child));
 				of_detach_node(child);
 				dev_err(parent, "%s: Device driver will not be probed, error: %d\n",
 					child->full_name, err);
-- 
2.53.0

